# ── Reports (generated, not tracked) ─────────────────────────────────
docs/*
api/docs/*
# Review and incident records (`docs/review/`, `api/docs/review/`) were
# un-ignored here as a directory until the 2026-11-11 history scrub. They are
# internal documents: write them to ~/xcelsior-internal-docs, outside the
# repository. The block at the end of this file keeps them out, and
# tests/test_internal_documents_are_not_tracked.py fails if one is tracked.
#
# The principle that exemption stated still holds for what remains below: an
# incident write-up that silently is not in the repository is worth less than
# no write-up, because it reads as done. So a document shipped code cites is
# either exempted here or not cited.
!docs/reconciliation.md
!api/docs/reconciliation.md
# Cited by shipped source, so they cannot stay local-only. `docs/*` above had
# swallowed all three: `scheduler.py`, `control_plane/scheduler/preference.py`,
# `control_plane/scheduler/migration_gate.py` and **migration 105** all point a
# reader at `placement-preference-plan.md` §-numbers, and a migration's comment
# is permanent history. A clone follows those pointers to nothing.
#
# This is the failure the comment above predicts — a document that "silently is
# not in the repository … reads as done" — reached through code references
# rather than through someone forgetting an exemption.
#
# `docs/BUSINESS_STRATEGY.md` is deliberately **not** here. It is cited too, but
# it is a business document and publishing it is not a call to make while
# tidying references.
!docs/3060-utilization-plan.md
!api/docs/3060-utilization-plan.md
!docs/placement-preference-plan.md
!api/docs/placement-preference-plan.md
!docs/pipeline-plan.md
